  "scope": "Stage4J6: recorded and captured D3D9 stateblocks use private holds for2D/cube/volume textures,VB/IB,declaration,VS/PS. Live and recorded slots publish before releasing replaced storage; final block cleanup detaches pointers before private release, then frees block before device pin. Capture is invalid while recording, matching existing Apply guard and Windows/Wine tests. Actual native methods with constructor/scalar-emitter stubs:160909 new checks,512 pool/final-owner profiles,4096 capture-clear-apply cycles,eight families,recorded kind/FVF replacement,recapture replacement,empty capture,recording guards,cancellation and final cleanup.35 strict assertion mutants,three old actual production/Capture/guard controls,ASAN/UBSAN. XP records all eight families,leaves public refs zero and performs65 Captures,528 getter queries,64 metadata rounds,two successful Applies and two recording refusals. Stateblock-only DEFAULT storage survives Reset and actual Apply; replacement Capture retires original eight resources; releasing block preserves live replacement eight until explicit unbind.16 resources,six exact buffer uploads,four programmable indexed draws,one clear,two successful Resets,five simulated XP transport readbacks; independent dual GPU320-pixel replay and empty guest maps before genuine owner release. Scalar-state algorithms,all predefined scope classes and sample filtering remain covered by retained independent tests; texture resources here are bound but not sampled by the color-only PS. General external-child device-root state retention,D3D8,arbitrary callbacks/thread/loss/full Reset/format/MSAA/fullscreen/multi-buffer/wrapper conversion,native HAL,games/FPS and overall stages4/5/6 remain open. Host/protocol/shader/bundle and D3D8/DDraw unchanged.",
